{
  "text": "2005B03 Write\nbrief short notes on the physicochemical properties of lignocaine.\nStructure\n·\nLipophilic modified benzene ring, amide chain,\n  terminal amine N(C2H5)2\n·\nAchiral\n·\nMolecular weight 234g/mols\nBehaviour\n·\nWeak base\no\npKa 7.9\no\nECF pH: 25% unionised\no\nICF pH: <10% unionised\n·\nLipid solubility 150x procaine\nAdditives\n·\nHCl: ↓pH -> ↑ionisation -> ↑solubility\n·\nSodium metabisulfite:\n  antioxidant/antibacterial (can cause hypersensitivity)\nFormulation\n·\nAqueous solution for injection\n·\nSolution for spray onto upper airway\n·\nTopical gel\n·\nWith prilocaine as EMLA\nFeedback welcome\nat\nketaminenightmares@gmail.com",
